# Ingress: the Cloudflare dashboard side

Worktree sites are `https://<label>.{{ hades_domain }}`, label `{{ hades_label_template }}`.
A Cloudflare Tunnel carries them to Caddy on `http://{{ ingress_loopback_address }}:{{ caddy_port }}`.

## 1. Tunnel

Zero Trust, Networks, Tunnels: create a cloudflared tunnel and copy its token.
Add one public hostname:

- Hostname: `*.{{ hades_domain }}`
- Service: `http://{{ ingress_loopback_address }}:{{ caddy_port }}`

DNS needs a proxied `*.{{ hades_domain }}` CNAME to the tunnel; add it if the dashboard did not.

## 2. Access application

Create a self-hosted application on `*.{{ hades_domain }}` with these paths:

- `dev`, `dev/*`
- `tidewave`, `tidewave/*`
- `phoenix/live_reload`, `phoenix/live_reload/*`

Give it a policy that admits only the team{% if cloudflare_team_domain is defined %} (team domain `{{ cloudflare_team_domain }}`){% endif %}.
Caddy answers 403 on these paths when the `Cf-Access-Jwt-Assertion` header is missing.
It checks only that the header is present, so the application must keep covering every path.

## 3. Connector

From the collection's `ansible/` directory on the controller:

    CLOUDFLARE_TUNNEL_TOKEN=… ansible-playbook -i inventory.yml playbooks/site.yml --tags ingress
